      "evidence": "Each blade lift actuator’s rod ends in an eye that a red long pin with stop bush (65304) takes, joining it to the blade (step 1137, book 2 page 342, https://www.lego.com/cdn/product-assets/product.bi.core.pdf/6403276.pdf#page=342; the actuator built with its rod and eye at step 408, book 1 page 305, https://www.lego.com/cdn/product-assets/product.bi.core.pdf/6403271.pdf#page=305). In the file the rod leans 2.0 degrees (0.035) in its submodel, so its eye is turned 2.01 degrees off the pin (p4271), past what the reading takes as one axis (2 degrees): the pin doesn’t go through the eye, and the rod hangs on nothing. Drawn straight along its cylinder, at the same distance out and the same side offset, the eye lies along the pin; it is then 7.7 LDU further along the pin, which the eye may slide along, and still on it."
